the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base income includes these resources:
    feel.

the functions are:
    the below household income limit of *a value* and *a second value* and *a third value* is *a fourth value*.

the knowledge base income includes:

the text of the_model is at "sources/Income.dmn".

the below household income limit of a value V and a value N and a third value is true if
    it is not the case that V < 0
    and it is not the case that
        N < 1
        or the count of the list the third value is a number M
            and N > M
            or it is not the case that N = floor(N)
    and the item at position N of the list the third value is a value K
    and V < K.

the below household income limit of a value V and a value N and a third value is false if
    it is not the case that V < 0
    and it is not the case that
        N < 1
        or the count of the list the third value is a number M
            and N > M
            or it is not the case that N = floor(N)
    and the item at position N of the list the third value is a value K
    and V >= K.

